<title>MALAYSIA: Westmont Land plans to buy Uganda bank.</title>
<headline>Westmont Land plans to buy Uganda bank.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Malaysian plantation and real estate group Westmont Land (Asia) Bhd said it was negotiating to buy a major stake in a commercial bank in Uganda.</p>
<p>It said in a statement late on Wednesday that it was also in the final stages of negotiating the purchase of a 100 mw barge-mounted power plant in Africa.</p>
<p>It did not give any details in the statement to the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Westmont said the statement was an interim announcement. Details would be announced once the deals were completed.</p>
<p>The share has been suspended since June 19. It was last traded at 3.52 ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
